  "term": "TSS",
  "definition": "TSS stands for transcutaneous spinal stimulation, a method that delivers stimulation through the skin over the spine. In the source, it is described as a way to help activate leg extensor muscles and support self-assisted standing in people with paralysis, sometimes used together with neuromuscular electrical stimulation.",
